<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21136" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hȳlaeus</span></b> , i, m.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὑλαῖος</span> (v. Chandler, Gr. Accent.
		§ 239). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A centaur who offered violence to Atalanta</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Ov. A.
				A. 2, 191</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 8, 294</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hylaeus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of Hylœus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ramus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					1, 1, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 6, 74</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ille etiam (i. e. Milanion) Hylaei percussus
					vulnere rami,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					1, 1, 13</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>One of Actœon's hounds</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 3,
				213</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab. 181</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
